{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>Whoever does not uphold.</b> Some say [it refers] to the entire Torah, and some say to those mentioned here, and they said nothing [further], because it is written \"to do them.\" But the correct view in my eyes is that [Scripture] pronounces a curse concerning the negative commandments mentioned, and pronounces a curse upon whoever does not keep even in secret a positive commandment; therefore it says \"to do them.\""], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:25:03.551040759Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}